WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.165
Week 20: Preterite and Imperfect Together. tell a coherent story explain circumstances identify cause and interruption

2
00:00:08.165 --> 00:00:21.601
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can tell a coherent story, explain circumstances, identify cause and interruption. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:29.169
Language system. Foreground versus background; interruption; bounded versus ongoing events; narrative viewpoint.

4
00:00:29.169 --> 00:00:35.221
Sound and delivery. Use pausing and prominence to separate background from main events.

5
00:00:35.221 --> 00:00:44.391
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:44.391 --> 00:01:13.401
Model language. Caminaba a casa cuando empezó la tormenta. — I was walking home when the storm started. Mientras todos dormían, sonó la alarma. — While everyone slept, the alarm went off. Ya había poca luz cuando llegamos. — There was already little light when we arrived. De repente, un vecino abrió la puerta. — Suddenly, a neighbor opened the door. Al final resolvimos el problema juntos. — In the end we solved the problem together.

7
00:01:13.401 --> 00:01:23.150
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
